            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "engine/review/app/verify.go validates the feature and the stored result name (review.CheckFeature, review.VerdictName) before it asks git or the store for anything. The tests in engine/review/app/verify_test.go cover traversal-style and empty names and check that no call is made. I found no path-injection route.",
              "The reply size is capped (review.MaxReplyBytes) before parsing, and the reply is parsed against the stored result's binding. A malformed or oversized reply stores nothing.",
              "The verdict is written through s.results.Create, which reports ErrExists when a file is already there. An existing verdict therefore cannot be overwritten, and ErrAlreadyVerified is returned.",
              "The correction-round check fails closed. If a stored verdict or the directory listing cannot be read, a blocking verdict is refused rather than allowed. There is a possible race where two concurrent blocking Verify calls on different heads both pass the spentRound check. The effect is only an extra correction round, with no data exposure, authorization bypass or loss, so I report no reachable security impact.",
              "The change adds no new dependencies and no secrets, and no sensitive data is logged or exposed."
            ]
          }
        }
