            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed both changed paths in full. Verify validates the feature, result name and reply size before calling git or the store, so a bad input fails fast with no side effects.",
              "The verdict is created through s.results.Create, which reports ErrExists as ErrAlreadyVerified. A retry after a successful store is therefore safe, and the existing verdict is never overwritten (engine/review/app/verify.go:104-114).",
              "ErrNotFlushed is surfaced in Verified.NotFlushed and the verdict is reported as stored, so a retry is not invited and no duplicate is created.",
              "spentRound fails closed: an unreadable or unparseable sibling verdict, or a directory that cannot be listed, stops a blocking verdict with a named cause, and nothing is stored. This is documented behavior and covered by tests.",
              "The extra reads in spentRound are O(number of verdicts in one feature directory) and run only when the decision is Blocks. No measured or realistic latency impact is shown.",
              "The check in spentRound followed by Create is not atomic across concurrent Verify calls on different results of the same base. I could not show that realistic callers run concurrently, so this is speculation and not a reportable finding."
            ]
          }
        }
